{"name":"Prairie Denim","hex":"#516678","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"prairie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An extensive area of relatively flat grassland with few, if any, trees, especially in North America."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prairie"},{"term":"denim","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A textile often made of cotton with a distinct diagonal pattern."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/denim"}],"entries":[{"title":"Prairie","blocks":[{"text":"Prairies are ecosystems considered part of the temperate grasslands, savannas, and shrublands biome by ecologists, based on similar temperate climates, moderate rainfall, and a composition of grasses, herbs, and shrubs, rather than trees, as the dominant vegetation type. Temperate grassland regions include the Pampas of Argentina, Brazil, and Uruguay, and the steppe of Romania, Ukraine, Russia, and Kazakhstan. Lands typically referred to as \"prairie\" tend to be in North America. The term encompasses the lower and mid-latitude of the area referred to as the Interior Plains of Canada, the United States, and Mexico. It includes all of the Great Plains as well as the wetter, hillier land to the east. From west to east, generally the drier expanse of shortgrass prairie gives way to mixed grass prairie and ultimately the richer and wetter soils of the tallgrass prairie."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/James_Woodworth_Prairie.jpg/330px-James_Woodworth_Prairie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prairie","wikidata":"Q194281"},{"title":"Denim","blocks":[{"text":"Denim is a sturdy, cotton, warp-faced textile in which the weft passes under two or more warp threads. This twill weave produces a diagonal ribbing that distinguishes it from cotton duck. Denim, as it is recognised today, was first produced in Nîmes, France."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Denim_texture_03.jpg/330px-Denim_texture_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denim","wikidata":"Q652698"},{"title":"List of colors: A–F","blocks":[{"text":"The following is a list of colors. A number of the color swatches below are taken from domain-specific naming schemes such as X11 or HTML4. RGB values are given for each swatch because such standards are defined in terms of the sRGB color space. It is not possible to accurately convert many of these swatches to CMYK values because of the differing gamuts of the two spaces, but the color management systems built into operating systems and image editing software attempt such conversions as accurately as possible."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Colouring_pencils.jpg/330px-Colouring_pencils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_colors%3A_A%E2%80%93F","wikidata":"Q16912543"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Wildflowers_on_Blackland_Prairie.jpg/500px-Wildflowers_on_Blackland_Prairie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Wildflowers_on_Blackland_Prairie.jpg/1280px-Wildflowers_on_Blackland_Prairie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Wildflowers_on_Blackland_Prairie.jpg/500px-Wildflowers_on_Blackland_Prairie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWildflowers_on_Blackland_Prairie.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/WY_Redds_Great_plains.jpg/500px-WY_Redds_Great_plains.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&ut